  "term": "antisocial personality disorder",
  "definition": "Antisocial personality disorder is a personality disorder marked by a long-standing pattern of disregarding and violating other people’s rights, beginning in childhood or early adolescence and continuing into adulthood. The diagnosis applies to someone who is at least 18 years old and who had some conduct disorder symptoms before age 15.",
